@meeting train.m18.calder
// SW3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5, S5-4): M18 Shutdowns, Thursday Day 18, 09:00-12:00, the Deck 6 port junction (j).
// Calder beside you at the planning screen (the Works app's Shutdowns tab opens after it, each step named): who it
// feeds, a quiet hour, who to warn; Brennan in person if it's the galley. One choice. Her step words while you plan are
// her own lines, flags train.m18.follow.*.
title: Shutdowns
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder showed you how to plan a shutdown: what a junction feeds, a quiet hour, who to warn, and what keeps power. You booked a real one for tomorrow.
== lines
calder > you: Your device. Works app. There's a new tab now. Shutdowns.   [gesture]
calder: Some Tier 3 jobs need the power off. You don't switch it off. You book it.
calder: First, what it feeds. Read the rooms. Then tomorrow's hours, and who's in them.
calder: Pick a quiet hour. Mealtimes and classes are marked. You can pick them. You'll hear about it.
calder: Warn the people it touches. The galley, you tell Brennan to her face. Always.
calder: Then what keeps power. The cold store, if it's the galley. You'll learn which.
? choice
* What if nobody's ever quiet?   rel:calder+2
  calder: Somebody always is. Mid-morning. Mid-afternoon. Look harder.   [nod]
* Why tell people in person? There's a notice.   rel:calder+2
  calder: A notice tells them. A person tells them you thought about them. They remember that.   [nod]
* (Just listen)
  calder: Good. Your turn.   [nod]
calder: Book it for tomorrow. At 22:00 it's settled. Then the ship plans round you. Don't miss your hour.
